.TH MEDIACONV 1 "2026-10-28" "mediaconv 5.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mediaconv \- batch-convert images, video and audio to widely compatible formats
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mediaconv.py
(\fB\-c\fR | \fB\-r\fR) [\fIFORMAT\fR...] [\fIOPTION\fR...]
.br
.B mediaconv.py
\fB\-v\fR | \fB\-h\fR | \fB\-\-check\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mediaconv
scans the current directory (or a whole tree) for files in the selected source
formats and converts them to JPG, WebP, MP4, MP3 or M4A.
Images are handled with Pillow, video and audio with ffmpeg.
Work is spread over threads, with the worker count chosen from the system load.
.PP
Source files are matched by extension, case-insensitively.
Output is written next to the source file.
Each output is first written to a temporary
.I .part
file and moved into place only when the conversion succeeded,
so a failure never leaves a truncated result.
A source is never deleted
.RB ( \-d )
unless its conversion succeeded.
.PP
At least one scope switch and at least one format switch are required.
.SH SCOPE
One of these is required.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-C ", " \-\-current
Process the current directory only.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-R ", " \-\-recursive
Include subdirectories.
.SH FORMAT SELECTORS
.TP
.B \-\-images
All image formats:
.BR \-\-png ,
.BR \-\-webp ,
.BR \-\-bmp ,
.BR \-\-tiff ,
.BR \-\-ico ,
.BR \-\-heic .
With
.B \-\-image\-to webp
the set is the same minus
.B \-\-webp
and plus
.BR \-\-jpg .
.TP
.B \-\-videos
All video formats, including
.BR \-\-ts
(note that .ts is also the TypeScript extension).
With
.B \-\-extract\-audio
or
.B \-\-merge
it also includes
.BR \-\-mp4 .
.TP
.B \-\-audio
All audio formats
.RB ( \-\-wma ,
.BR \-\-flac ,
.BR \-\-wav ,
.BR \-\-ogg ,
and
.B \-\-m4a
unless
.B \-\-audio\-to aac
is given).
.SH IMAGE FORMATS
.TP
.B \-\-gifi
Extract the first frame of a GIF as an image
.RI ( .jpg ,
or
.I .webp
with
.BR \-\-image\-to ).
Never selected by
.BR \-\-images .
Can be combined with
.BR \-\-gifv .
.TP
.B \-\-jpeg
Rename
.I .jpeg
to
.I .jpg
(no conversion).
.TP
.B \-\-jpg
Convert
.I .jpg
and
.I .jpeg
to WebP.
Requires
.BR "\-\-image\-to webp" .
.TP
.B \-\-png \-\-bmp \-\-ico
Convert to the image target format.
.B \-\-ico
uses the largest size in the file.
.TP
.B \-\-webp
Convert WebP to JPG.
Cannot be combined with
.BR "\-\-image\-to webp" .
.TP
.B \-\-tiff
Convert
.I .tif
and
.I .tiff
(first page only).
.TP
.B \-\-heic
Convert
.I .heic
and
.IR .heif .
Requires the pillow-heif package.
.SH VIDEO FORMATS
All video formats produce
.I .mp4
(H.264 video and AAC audio by default).
.TP
.B \-\-webm \-\-wmv \-\-avi \-\-flv \-\-mov \-\-mkv \-\-m4v \-\-3gp
Convert the named container.
.TP
.B \-\-mpg
.I .mpg
and
.IR .mpeg .
.TP
.B \-\-ts
.IR .ts ,
.I .mts
and
.IR .m2ts .
Also selected by
.BR \-\-videos .
.TP
.B \-\-gifv
Convert an animated GIF to a silent MP4.
Never selected by
.BR \-\-videos .
If
.B \-\-gifi
is also given, static GIFs are left to it.
After
.B \-d
such a GIF is deleted only when both outputs were written.
.TP
.B \-\-mp4
Source for
.B \-\-extract\-audio
or
.B \-\-merge
only.
.SH AUDIO FORMATS
.TP
.B \-\-wma \-\-flac \-\-wav \-\-ogg \-\-m4a
Convert to MP3, or to AAC in
.I .m4a
with
.BR "\-\-audio\-to aac" .
.B \-\-m4a
as a source cannot be combined with
.BR "\-\-audio\-to aac" .
.SH IMAGE OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-image\-to " FORMAT"
Target image format:
.B jpg
(default) or
.BR webp .
.TP
.BI \-\-quality " N"
Image quality, 1\-100.
Default 95 for JPG and 90 for WebP.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-size " PX"
Shrink images so the longest side is at most
.I PX
pixels.
Smaller images are left alone.
.TP
.B \-\-strip\-metadata
Drop EXIF and GPS metadata.
Metadata is kept by default, and EXIF orientation is always applied to the pixels.
.PP
Transparency is flattened onto white for JPG and kept for WebP.
.SH VIDEO OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-h265
Encode H.265/HEVC instead of H.264.
.TP
.BI \-\-crf " N"
Quality, lower is better.
Default 23 for H.264 and 28 for H.265.
For hardware encoders it is mapped to the encoder's constant-quality setting.
.TP
.BI \-\-preset " NAME"
Software encoder speed, from
.B ultrafast
to
.BR veryslow .
Default
.BR medium .
.TP
.BI \-\-hw " ENCODER"
Use a hardware encoder:
.BR nvenc ,
.BR qsv
or
.BR amf .
Fails with a message if the installed ffmpeg lacks it.
.TP
.B \-\-remux
For mkv, mov, ts, m4v, 3gp and mpg sources, copy the streams into MP4 without
re-encoding.
Audio that MP4 cannot carry is converted to AAC;
if the video codec does not fit MP4, or the copy fails, the file is re-encoded.
Requires
.BR ffprobe .
.SH MERGE
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-M ", " \-\-merge
Join the videos of each folder into one MP4 named
.IB folder _merged.mp4
in that folder, in natural name order (clip2 before clip10).
With
.BR \-r ,
every subfolder is merged separately.
Folders with a single video, and earlier
.I *_merged.mp4
outputs, are skipped.
All clips are scaled to fit the largest frame (by area) keeping their aspect
ratio, and padded with black in one or both dimensions where needed.
The frame rate is matched to the highest, audio is converted to a common
format, and clips without audio get silence.
Files that ffprobe cannot read as video are left out and kept.
Merging always re-encodes, so it cannot be combined with
.B \-\-remux
or
.BR \-\-extract\-audio ,
and needs
.BR ffprobe .
.PP
With
.BR \-d ,
a warning states how many source files may be deleted and asks for confirmation
unless
.B \-\-yes
is given; declining cancels the run.
Sources are deleted only after their folder was merged successfully.
.SH AUDIO OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-audio\-to " FORMAT"
Audio target:
.B mp3
(default) or
.B aac
(written as
.IR .m4a ).
.TP
.BI \-\-abitrate " RATE"
Audio bitrate, for example
.BR 192k .
Default
.BR 192k .
.TP
.B \-\-extract\-audio
Video sources produce audio files instead of MP4.
A video without an audio track is reported as an error and its source is kept.
.SH BEHAVIOR
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-O ", " \-\-overwrite
Overwrite existing output.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-S ", " \-\-skip\-existing
Skip a file when its output already exists.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-D ", " \-\-delete\-source
Delete the source after a successful conversion.
With
.B \-\-merge
a warning and confirmation come first.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-N ", " \-\-dry\-run
Show what would happen without converting anything.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-L ", " \-\-log
Write the activity log
.IR mediaconv.log .
Errors are logged regardless, see
.BR FILES .
.PP
.B \-\-overwrite
and
.B \-\-skip\-existing
cannot be combined.
With neither, a name conflict is resolved by appending
.IR _001 ,
.IR _002 ,
and so on to the output name, and the existing file is left untouched.
.SH PREREQUISITES
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-Y ", " \-\-yes
Allow installing missing prerequisites without asking.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-install
Never offer to install anything.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Print the status of Pillow, pillow-heif, ffmpeg, ffprobe and the hardware
encoders, then exit.
.PP
Only what the selected files need is checked, after the files have been found.
If something is missing,
.B mediaconv
shows the exact install command and asks for confirmation.
Without a terminal and without
.B \-\-yes
nothing is installed.
Dry runs skip the check.
.PP
Installers used:
.B pip
for Pillow and pillow-heif;
.B winget
(Windows),
.B brew
(macOS), or
.BR apt\-get ,
.BR dnf ,
.B pacman
or
.B zypper
through
.B sudo
(Linux) for ffmpeg.
.SH HELP
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-H ", " \-\-help
Show the full switch list, headed by the version.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.PP
Every single-letter switch is accepted in either case.
A malformed command line prints the version, a short usage line and the error.
.SH OUTPUT
The console shows per-type file counts, a
.B Processing:
line per file, and a final summary.
On a terminal, a live status line shows
.B x of y files processed
plus the percent done of each active ffmpeg job (percentages need
.BR ffprobe ).
When output is redirected, one
.B [x/y] name
line is printed per finished file instead.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I mediaconv.errors.log
Written in the working directory whenever an error occurs, with or without
.BR \-\-log .
Created on the first error, so it exists only if something failed.
.TP
.I mediaconv.log
Written in the working directory only with
.BR \-\-log .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, or no matching files.
.TP
.B 1
One or more conversions failed, or a prerequisite is missing.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command line.
.SH EXAMPLES
Convert PNG and WebP files in the current directory to JPG:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mediaconv.py \-c \-\-png \-\-webp
.fi
.RE
.PP
Convert every image under the current tree to WebP:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mediaconv.py \-r \-\-images \-\-image\-to webp
.fi
.RE
.PP
Turn all videos into MP4, copying streams where possible, and delete the originals:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mediaconv.py \-r \-\-videos \-\-remux \-d
.fi
.RE
.PP
Re-encode MKV files as H.265:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mediaconv.py \-r \-\-mkv \-\-h265 \-\-crf 26
.fi
.RE
.PP
Extract MP3 audio from MP4 files:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mediaconv.py \-c \-\-mp4 \-\-extract\-audio
.fi
.RE
.PP
Preview resizing HEIC photos to JPG without changing anything:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mediaconv.py \-r \-\-heic \-\-max\-size 2048 \-n
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR ffprobe (1)
